WEBVTT

00:25.066 --> 00:27.694
It's breeding season for the scalewolves.

00:28.403 --> 00:31.197
So they don't hurt their pups
who are soon to be born,

00:31.281 --> 00:35.410
they're shedding their hard-scaled fur
by ramming their bodies together.

00:36.661 --> 00:38.580
If they never took a mate,

00:39.164 --> 00:41.332
they could remain strong.

00:44.919 --> 00:48.256
I thought a girl like her
would have nothing to offer me.

00:49.507 --> 00:51.509
That an Outsider is an outsider.

00:52.010 --> 00:54.637
That they had no place
in the world of magic.

00:56.639 --> 00:57.515
But,

00:58.516 --> 01:01.186
if she learns the rules the right way,

01:01.686 --> 01:05.857
then what is the difference
between her and us?

02:44.581 --> 02:46.708
Yes! I did it!

02:46.791 --> 02:48.168
That's great!

02:48.251 --> 02:49.377
THE TRIAL AT SERPENTBACK CAVE

02:49.460 --> 02:52.589
You're drawing
much more stable spells now, Coco.

02:52.672 --> 02:54.048
Thank you.

02:55.133 --> 02:56.467
Still,

02:56.551 --> 03:00.138
there aren't many spells
I can use with confidence yet.

03:00.638 --> 03:04.017
So when something happens suddenly,
I always fall back on the same ones.

03:06.060 --> 03:07.854
If you ask me,

03:08.438 --> 03:10.398
the spells you rarely mess up,

03:10.481 --> 03:13.109
the ones you draw without thinking,

03:13.693 --> 03:15.778
are probably your strengths.

03:19.449 --> 03:22.202
My strengths?

03:22.702 --> 03:23.745
Yes.

03:24.704 --> 03:25.538
See?

03:25.622 --> 03:26.998
The spells you use often?

03:27.081 --> 03:29.876
You can see
you rely heavily on straight lines.

03:30.376 --> 03:34.756
Compared to curves,
your straight lines never waver.

03:35.590 --> 03:38.009
The first thing you showed me when we met

03:38.092 --> 03:40.386
was how beautifully
you could draw a straight line.

03:42.847 --> 03:45.141
When you're aware of your strengths,

03:45.225 --> 03:49.520
they become a source of confidence to
lean on when it's time to trust yourself.

03:50.521 --> 03:54.525
When you're feeling uncertain,
say it out loud. Let yourself hear it.

03:56.736 --> 03:58.446
My strength

03:59.155 --> 04:00.740
is drawing straight lines.

04:01.866 --> 04:05.161
So my strength is drawing straight lines!

04:05.745 --> 04:07.997
Then all that's left is practice!

04:08.498 --> 04:11.084
Draw straighter.
I'll keep going straight ahead!

04:11.167 --> 04:12.669
Hold on there!

04:13.795 --> 04:17.006
The spells you're good at
will improve on their own.

04:18.007 --> 04:20.385
You need to practice the ones
you wouldn't normally use.

04:21.594 --> 04:24.013
The spells you still can't draw.

04:24.514 --> 04:27.558
You might discover a new strength.

04:28.768 --> 04:29.602
Right?

04:30.520 --> 04:32.188
Okay...

04:37.402 --> 04:38.444
Somehow,

04:38.528 --> 04:42.115
seals look even more incredible to me now
than they did before.

04:47.537 --> 04:49.747
Now that I know how they're created,

04:50.248 --> 04:52.625
I can tell just how difficult
they really are.

04:53.876 --> 04:57.088
I've started to see that now.

04:59.215 --> 05:00.216
Amazing.

05:00.883 --> 05:02.468
This is amazing.

05:02.969 --> 05:04.929
The spells of amazing people are amazing.

05:05.013 --> 05:07.724
Your vocabulary for praise
is severely lacking.

05:08.599 --> 05:11.185
It's so amazing
it's actually kind of discouraging.

05:11.811 --> 05:13.479
Richeh, wanna take a look too?

05:14.856 --> 05:15.898
No.

05:18.401 --> 05:21.988
I like drawing them,
but I don't like looking at them.

05:22.989 --> 05:24.699
Really? You're not gonna look?

05:25.199 --> 05:27.493
I said no. And your movement is annoying.

05:31.122 --> 05:35.460
Magic isn't just about putting pen
to paper, Richeh.

05:37.128 --> 05:41.132
Studying exceptional magic
is how you train your eye--

05:41.215 --> 05:42.633
I said I don't want to look!

05:44.218 --> 05:46.179
Richeh! Are you all right?

05:46.262 --> 05:47.597
Are you hurt?

05:49.474 --> 05:52.310
Using magic in a fit of anger
isn't exactly admirable.

05:52.393 --> 05:53.519
It's dangerous.

05:58.691 --> 06:00.109
Wait, Richeh.

06:04.864 --> 06:07.658
If you keep turning your eyes away from
what could teach you

06:07.742 --> 06:10.661
and stop listening to your master's words,

06:11.996 --> 06:14.248
you'll never get anywhere.

06:22.131 --> 06:24.300
Um, I'm sorry about earlier.

06:25.093 --> 06:26.135
I...

06:30.473 --> 06:32.517
Huh? Richeh?

06:33.935 --> 06:35.103
She's not here?

06:37.480 --> 06:38.856
Is she in her bedroom?

06:44.654 --> 06:46.781
You know where she is, Brushbuddy?

06:52.703 --> 06:53.955
What?!

06:54.038 --> 06:55.581
Where are you going, Brushbuddy?

06:57.667 --> 06:58.918
Huh?!

07:07.969 --> 07:09.137
Brushbuddy?

07:10.179 --> 07:12.098
Where is this place?

07:36.080 --> 07:38.332
Wow.

07:40.001 --> 07:42.003
I didn't say you could come in.

07:42.086 --> 07:43.504
Oh, I'm sorry.

07:43.588 --> 07:45.298
I was following Brushbuddy.

07:45.798 --> 07:47.592
What a beautiful spell.

07:47.675 --> 07:49.760
It's like a ribbon made of crystal.

07:53.598 --> 07:55.349
It doesn't have a name yet.

07:55.850 --> 07:57.018
I made it.

07:57.101 --> 07:59.145
It's your own original spell?

07:59.937 --> 08:02.148
Wow, that's amazing.

08:03.316 --> 08:06.319
It's so gorgeous. It makes my eyes happy.

08:06.402 --> 08:08.488
That's a unique way
to appreciate something.

08:10.740 --> 08:13.409
I really like this spell.

08:21.417 --> 08:23.586
- If you want one, you can have it.
- What?!

08:24.086 --> 08:25.254
I've got plenty anyway.

08:25.338 --> 08:26.672
What?! Really?

08:29.550 --> 08:30.384
I'm so happy.

08:30.885 --> 08:32.094
Thank you!

08:34.305 --> 08:35.306
Hey.

08:36.682 --> 08:38.142
Can I ask you something?

08:39.602 --> 08:42.104
Why don't you like to look at books?

08:44.357 --> 08:47.401
I don't really know much about magic,

08:47.485 --> 08:49.737
so I love reading books about it.

08:51.155 --> 08:53.699
Who created each spell and when?

08:53.783 --> 08:55.284
What made them want to cast it?

08:55.785 --> 08:59.372
I like imagining those things as I read.

09:04.126 --> 09:08.256
I only want to think about my own magic.

09:10.633 --> 09:12.343
When I read those books,

09:12.426 --> 09:16.681
the next thing is they tell me to try
drawing the same spells.

09:17.348 --> 09:19.684
They make me draw things
I don't want to draw.

09:20.184 --> 09:22.186
Magic that isn't my type of magic.

09:23.271 --> 09:24.730
I'm sick of it.

09:27.525 --> 09:29.652
It doesn't concern you, Coco.

09:30.653 --> 09:32.613
I don't need anyone else's magic.

09:33.114 --> 09:36.158
I don't want my magic to be tainted.

09:37.952 --> 09:40.329
Before coming here,

09:40.413 --> 09:44.041
Richeh already ended her apprenticeship
with another witch.

09:44.542 --> 09:48.296
That stubbornness of hers
is a shield she uses to protect herself.

09:48.879 --> 09:52.216
Like a scalewolf armored in hard fur...

09:52.800 --> 09:54.594
It's hard to know how far to push.

09:56.470 --> 10:00.391
People aren't as simple as magic.

10:02.435 --> 10:03.436
Here.

10:03.519 --> 10:04.645
What's this?

10:07.315 --> 10:08.357
A rock?

10:08.441 --> 10:12.111
My latest original spell, the Snugstone.

10:12.695 --> 10:14.655
Keep it in your bed,

10:14.739 --> 10:18.743
and it should keep you warm to your toes
and help you sleep soundly.

10:18.826 --> 10:22.705
It may just be a placebo,
but give them to the apprentices for me.

10:23.914 --> 10:24.957
Thanks.

10:25.791 --> 10:28.127
Your magic is kind.

10:28.961 --> 10:30.504
It says more than words ever could.

10:30.588 --> 10:33.799
It's just work-related!

10:33.883 --> 10:38.179
It's a prototype I'm developing for sale.
I just want feedback, that's all!

10:38.679 --> 10:40.890
Sure, whatever you say.

10:46.854 --> 10:48.397
- Hey, Olru.
- Hmm?

10:48.981 --> 10:51.275
There are too many. There's five.

10:53.277 --> 10:54.862
Four are for the apprentices.

10:56.739 --> 10:58.908
The last one is for you.

11:01.160 --> 11:04.330
At least set an example
and get some sleep at night.

11:07.291 --> 11:08.626
You're their master.

11:15.299 --> 11:16.592
I'll try.

11:20.513 --> 11:21.806
A letter?

11:22.431 --> 11:23.516
I wonder who it's from.

11:27.645 --> 11:29.355
I'm back.

11:30.981 --> 11:31.982
Agott.

11:33.025 --> 11:35.361
Perfect timing.

11:35.861 --> 11:37.697
I just got word from the Great Hall.

11:38.322 --> 11:40.449
The date for the second exam has been set.

11:41.242 --> 11:42.576
When is it?

11:42.660 --> 11:44.662
Three days from now, at dawn.

11:45.830 --> 11:48.833
Serpentback Cave on Cape Romonon.

11:57.550 --> 12:00.344
You want to make crystal ribbons?

12:02.138 --> 12:05.266
That's such an adorable spell, Richelitte.

12:08.811 --> 12:09.729
- Hmph!
- Hey!

12:17.319 --> 12:18.487
Look, Riri.

12:21.073 --> 12:23.617
It's twinkly and sparkly. So pretty!

12:34.879 --> 12:36.255
Riri?

12:37.506 --> 12:38.883
You know, I...

12:39.467 --> 12:42.636
love the magic that makes you you, Richeh.

12:44.513 --> 12:47.725
So please, stay just as you are.

12:50.561 --> 12:51.645
Riri?

12:52.813 --> 12:54.023
Where are you going?

12:54.732 --> 12:57.651
Aren't you going to watch
my magic anymore?

12:58.152 --> 13:01.071
Don't go, Riri.

13:08.078 --> 13:09.246
A dream...

13:11.040 --> 13:14.293
I slept like a log.

13:14.919 --> 13:18.798
I was planning to practice right up until
the last minute before the exam.

13:19.381 --> 13:22.843
But because of this cozy Snugstone...

13:22.927 --> 13:24.303
Yeah.

13:24.386 --> 13:26.096
Don't worry, Agott.

13:27.097 --> 13:31.018
No matter how much you prepare,
everyone feels like it isn't enough.

13:32.144 --> 13:34.104
Just do your best as you are now.

13:35.356 --> 13:37.525
For the sake
of who you'll become next time.

13:41.111 --> 13:43.030
There won't be a next time.

13:49.745 --> 13:51.872
I'll pass it on my first try.

13:51.956 --> 13:54.458
After all, I'm a member of House Arklaum.

13:54.542 --> 13:57.419
My, my, how reassuring.

13:59.296 --> 14:02.550
She's worlds apart
from the underachiever in my care.

14:02.633 --> 14:04.426
My apprentice, Euini,

14:04.510 --> 14:07.972
has already failed the Second Exam twice

14:08.055 --> 14:10.933
when you can only apply once a year.

14:11.517 --> 14:13.310
I'd love to swap her dominant hand

14:13.394 --> 14:16.230
with that of a young lady
from the illustrious House Arklaum.

14:16.313 --> 14:17.565
Master Kukrow!

14:17.648 --> 14:21.402
Apprentices aren't objects.
You can't just swap them out.

14:21.485 --> 14:23.404
That's exactly the problem.

14:24.488 --> 14:26.574
You can't repair them either.

14:26.657 --> 14:28.617
You shouldn't talk that way...

14:28.701 --> 14:31.078
Oh, um, it's okay.

14:31.662 --> 14:33.914
It's all true.

14:33.998 --> 14:35.791
I'm a lousy apprentice.

14:35.875 --> 14:38.544
I've been nothing but a burden
to Master Kukrow.

14:38.627 --> 14:39.461
And,

14:39.545 --> 14:43.465
because I'm so incompetent, people
end up speaking badly about him too.

14:43.549 --> 14:44.466
I'm so sorry.

14:44.550 --> 14:45.551
Someone like me...

14:45.634 --> 14:48.095
Um, Euini?

14:48.178 --> 14:50.973
Man, I'm late. My bad.

14:51.056 --> 14:54.435
The nearest window-way wasn't working

14:54.518 --> 14:57.813
so I had to walk all the way here.

14:59.565 --> 15:02.860
The giant brushbuddy is talking!

15:03.444 --> 15:05.070
Take a closer look.

15:05.154 --> 15:07.781
She's a bona fide witch.

15:08.282 --> 15:11.493
Oh, but I thought transformations
are forbidden magic?

15:12.077 --> 15:14.330
The mirror cloak of Borrowshade.

15:14.830 --> 15:16.123
While you're wearing it,

15:16.206 --> 15:20.878
the contraption projects the illusion
of the beast standing in front of you.

15:22.087 --> 15:24.465
Nice to meet you. I'm Alaira.

15:24.965 --> 15:26.759
I'm one of the proctors

15:26.842 --> 15:29.011
overseeing the Second Exam.

15:29.595 --> 15:31.513
You're the proctor?

15:31.597 --> 15:32.806
What a coincidence.

15:33.307 --> 15:36.769
Looks like you brought everyone along.
Even those who aren't taking the exam.

15:37.603 --> 15:38.854
The second test,

15:38.938 --> 15:41.565
"The Sincerity of the Shield,"
is exactly how it sounds.

15:41.649 --> 15:44.485
Like a knight,
you'll be protecting a designated person

15:44.568 --> 15:46.904
and escorting them safely through
Serpentback Cave,

15:46.987 --> 15:49.531
from the entrance all the way to the exit.

15:49.615 --> 15:52.493
You fail if you lose sight
of who you're guarding.

15:52.576 --> 15:56.455
And you fail if only one of you reaches
the exit ahead of the other.

15:56.538 --> 16:00.542
Naturally, you're also disqualified
if anyone sees you drawing a spell.

16:01.043 --> 16:04.129
What if someone does see us?

16:04.213 --> 16:06.757
You won't have to worry about
the secret being exposed,

16:06.840 --> 16:09.051
but you'll fail the exam.

16:09.802 --> 16:11.679
Because they'll realize you're human.

16:12.179 --> 16:15.432
Put on that cloak and look through here.

16:26.777 --> 16:29.071
Is that a gryphon?

16:29.154 --> 16:31.573
No, those are myrphons.

16:32.074 --> 16:33.826
They're different species.

16:34.785 --> 16:37.162
The Serpentback Cave used for the exam

16:37.246 --> 16:39.707
is a magical ruin
dating back to the Age of Chaos.

16:40.207 --> 16:42.459
Inside, labyrinth magic swirls
through the passage.

16:42.543 --> 16:45.087
Stray from the path and you're in danger.

16:46.630 --> 16:50.217
So the Second Exam is about using magic

16:50.300 --> 16:52.219
to protect them from magic?

16:52.302 --> 16:53.762
Exactly.

16:53.846 --> 16:56.640
Humans rarely set foot
in those ruins anymore,

16:56.724 --> 16:59.893
but for the beasts, they've long served
as one of the migratory routes

16:59.977 --> 17:02.229
connecting their breeding
and wintering grounds.

17:02.312 --> 17:06.483
Witches bear responsibility
for changing their world.

17:09.653 --> 17:10.988
That's why, every year,

17:11.071 --> 17:14.199
we guide and escort the young ones
who've only just left the nest,

17:14.283 --> 17:17.703
so they don't lose their way.

17:17.786 --> 17:20.247
With the magic in those cloaks,

17:20.330 --> 17:23.584
myrphons should see you as members
of their own flock right now.

17:23.667 --> 17:26.670
But if you take the cloak off,
or if the seal gets damaged,

17:26.754 --> 17:28.672
they'll immediately bolt, so be careful.

17:29.256 --> 17:30.591
I see.

17:31.175 --> 17:36.597
So in a way, this is even harder than
drawing magic without humans noticing.

17:37.431 --> 17:39.433
You'll each be assigned one bird.

17:39.933 --> 17:41.602
This one's yours.

17:41.685 --> 17:43.353
And this one's yours.

17:44.104 --> 17:47.483
Right, and the last one goes to you.

17:50.694 --> 17:51.695
To Richeh?

17:52.196 --> 17:54.323
This is a mistake.

17:54.823 --> 17:56.784
I'm not taking the test.

17:57.284 --> 18:00.913
Oh? That's strange.
We have an application for you.

18:00.996 --> 18:02.623
It's not a mistake.

18:03.207 --> 18:05.709
You're taking the exam too, Richeh.

18:16.929 --> 18:18.138
Liar.

18:21.225 --> 18:23.018
Master Qifrey,

18:23.102 --> 18:26.063
you said I can do what I want.

18:26.855 --> 18:29.233
That's why I came to you.

18:29.817 --> 18:32.486
You don't care what I want either, do you?

18:32.986 --> 18:35.239
You'll make me do
whatever the adults want.

18:36.740 --> 18:38.742
It's not that I don't care.

18:39.868 --> 18:42.287
In fact, it's because I do care

18:42.371 --> 18:44.164
that I want you to take this exam.

18:44.957 --> 18:46.959
I think what you learn here

18:47.042 --> 18:49.837
will help you live the way
you want to live.

18:50.420 --> 18:51.255
So,

18:52.840 --> 18:55.259
will you trust me this time?

19:03.016 --> 19:06.562
During the exam,
I'm gonna do things how I want.

19:08.021 --> 19:09.857
Sure. Yes.

19:10.357 --> 19:11.191
That's fine.

19:11.775 --> 19:14.820
If I try it and hate it, I won't do it.

19:15.696 --> 19:17.906
If I stop being me.

19:18.407 --> 19:21.410
I'll never believe you again.

19:25.831 --> 19:29.251
Seems you have your hands full too.

19:29.334 --> 19:32.671
The hopeless ones stay hopeless
no matter what you say.

19:32.754 --> 19:35.632
They always have some excuse. "But... but..."

19:37.593 --> 19:40.387
It's exhausting, isn't it?

19:40.470 --> 19:42.472
- Why are children so--
- Excuse me.

19:43.640 --> 19:46.143
Did you just say something?

19:46.226 --> 19:47.436
Huh?

19:47.519 --> 19:50.147
Well then, look at the time.

19:50.230 --> 19:53.275
I'd better get back to the Great Hall.

19:54.484 --> 19:55.402
What?

19:55.485 --> 19:57.696
You're leaving your apprentice's exam?

19:57.779 --> 20:02.159
What? With you lot here, he'll be fine.

20:02.242 --> 20:04.828
I leave the rest to you.

20:08.373 --> 20:11.793
No way. He actually left.

20:12.628 --> 20:13.670
Euini.

20:14.254 --> 20:16.715
I'll try my best.

20:16.798 --> 20:19.384
Oh, yes, good luck.

20:25.599 --> 20:27.100
It's about time.

20:27.643 --> 20:31.521
If only everyone could find their way
through the darkness.

20:32.022 --> 20:33.690
That's what magic is for.

20:33.774 --> 20:35.234
Exactly for that.

20:46.036 --> 20:47.704
They're moving.

20:59.424 --> 21:01.176
Okay, then. Let's go!

21:23.365 --> 21:24.741
They've gone.

21:24.825 --> 21:28.203
Now then,
how about we grab a late breakfast?

21:28.704 --> 21:30.872
We can talk a little history
while we're at it.

21:30.956 --> 21:32.207
History?

21:32.708 --> 21:33.625
Yes.

21:34.209 --> 21:36.837
You're probably not very familiar
with magical ruins

21:36.920 --> 21:39.089
like Serpentback Cave yet, are you, Coco?

21:41.341 --> 21:44.511
About how the forbidden magic
created before The Day of the Pact...

21:46.972 --> 21:49.599
left a scar upon the world?

21:51.476 --> 21:53.979
We have to go down this path?

21:54.479 --> 21:55.647
I told you,

21:56.148 --> 21:58.900
this is an exam about protecting
against magic with magic.

21:59.776 --> 22:02.279
Now then, our young knights of magic,

22:02.362 --> 22:05.490
how will you proceed from here?

23:33.703 --> 23:35.914
Subtitle translation by: Emily Noguchi

23:36.873 --> 23:40.919
EPISODE 12
THE SHADOW OF ROMONON
